=== plain-80: width 80, height 24, profile notty, dark, glyphs ascii, plain
# play users/pve9 ----------------------------------------------$
$
# Note$
# Play mode: hardn's own screens and prompts, on the real$
# plan/apply engine against a simulated host, hostfake's$
# recording host.System, whose commands a model of the host$
# answers. Nothing on this machine changes: every command and$
# file is the fake's, and its record is shown when play ends.$
$
# Info: users/pve9$
# web-01.example.net is a Proxmox VE 9 node: root alone, by key$
# (brief 2.5), no sudo. hardn runs as root.$
$
# User Management ##############################################$
$
  [ ] User                 Not Configured root only$
$
# Users --------------------------------------------------------$
$
   -  No user besides root$
$
  Select an option$
$
   2) Create User          Configure a new user$
$
   0) Return$
$
    > Enter your choice [0, 2 or q]: 2$
$
# Create User ##################################################$
$
   1. Username [0 or q]: carol$
$
   2. Grant admin rights? [y/N, 0 or q]: y$
  (x) sudo isn't installed, so hardn can't grant admin rights.$
      Install sudo, then try again.$
   2. Grant admin rights? [y/N, 0 or q]: n$
$
   3. Add SSH key? [y/N, 0 or q]: n$
$
# User Configuration -------------------------------------------$
$
   -  Sudo                 Disabled$
  [ ] SSH Keys             None$
   -  Password             None$
  [ ] Without a key carol can't log in: there's no password$
$
   -  Create user carol$
      /etc/passwd$
      -absent$
      +no password, key login$
      $ useradd --home-dir /home/carol --create-home --shell$
      | /bin/bash carol$
$
  Create user 'carol'? [y/N, 0 or q]: y$
$
  [+] Create user carol    Done$
$
# Operation Successful$
$
# User Management ##############################################$
$
  [ ] User                 Partial non-root, no sudo$
$
# carol --------------------------------------------------------$
$
   -  Sudo                 Disabled$
  [ ] SSH Keys             None$
   -  Password             None$
$
  Select an option$
$
   1) Manage User          Configure sudo, SSH keys$
   2) Create User          Configure a new user$
$
   0) Return$
$
    > Enter your choice [0-2 or q]: 0$
$
# simulated system ---------------------------------------------$
$
# Info: users/pve9$
# Recorded by the fake, not done: what each step ran on web-$
# 01.example.net, and the files it changed, in order; hardn's$
# own journal, run directory and backups left out.$
$
   -  Applied: Create user carol$
      $ useradd --home-dir /home/carol --create-home --shell$
      | /bin/bash carol$
$

